StrongAuthIdpEntraS5               =In "Certificates & secrets" → New client secret → copy the secret VALUE immediately (it is shown only once).
StrongAuthIdpGoogleS1              =Open Google Cloud Console (button below) → APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen: User type = Internal, fill app name and your Workspace email. Save.
StrongAuthIdpGoogleS2              =Credentials → "Create credentials" → "OAuth client ID" → Application type: Web application.
StrongAuthIdpGoogleS3              =Under "Authorized redirect URIs" → Add URI → paste the Redirect URI shown below. Create.
StrongAuthIdpGoogleS4              =Copy the Client ID and Client secret shown after creation — you will paste them in Step 2.
StrongAuthIdpOidcS1                =Create a confidential OIDC client on your identity provider (Keycloak / Authentik / Okta ...) with the Redirect URI shown below and a client secret.
StrongAuthIdpOidcS2                =Copy the issuer URL, client ID and client secret for Step 2.
StrongAuthIdpGoogleGuide           =In Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials (configure the OAuth consent screen first, User type = Internal): "Create credentials" → "OAuth client ID" → Web application → add the redirect URI below; then copy the Client ID and Client secret.
StrongAuthIdpOidcGuide             =Create an OIDC client on your identity provider (Keycloak, Authentik, Okta, ...) with the redirect URI below, confidential client with a client secret. You only need the issuer URL plus the client credentials.
