# Admin setup — labels and help
StrongAuthIssuerNameHelp           =Issuer label embedded in TOTP QR codes (default: Dolibarr)
StrongAuthInternalDomainsHelp      =Comma-separated email domains that must use an external IdP (e.g. M365/Entra ID). Users with these domains bypass local password and TOTP requirements.
StrongAuthRequire2FALocalHelp      =Force TOTP second factor on every local-password login (recommended for external users).
StrongAuthRequire2FAIdpHelp        =Require a second factor from the IdP itself in addition to StrongAuth-managed factors (e.g. Microsoft Authenticator step-up).
StrongAuthMaxFailedHelp            =Number of consecutive failed 2FA attempts before the account is temporarily locked (1–50)
StrongAuthLockoutDurationHelp      =Lockout duration in seconds (60–86400). Default 900 = 15 minutes.
StrongAuthBackupCountHelp          =Backup codes generated per enrollment (1–50). Default 10.
StrongAuthDeviceTrustLocalHelp     =Allow users to mark a browser as trusted for 30 days (skips TOTP on that device). Off by default.
StrongAuthAdminBreakglassHelp      =Admin break-glass: Dolibarr admins may bypass the IdP-only rule with the local password. Keep ON until SSO is fully verified; turning it OFF enforces M365-only for admins too — an IdP outage then locks admins out (recovery: clear STRONGAUTH_INTERNAL_DOMAINS in the database).
StrongAuthAllowWebAuthnHelp        =Passkey as an extra step-up factor for internal-domain users, on top of the IdP's own MFA (also needs "Require a second factor from the IdP" = ON). Leave OFF when internal users are IdP-only — the IdP MFA already is their second factor.
StrongAuthWebAuthnRpIdHelp         =WebAuthn relying-party ID. Defaults to the HTTP_HOST; override only when running behind a proxy that mangles the host header.

